# A/B (ENV held): OCT- keeps the sound as A, OCT+ as B, SELECT walks from one to the other, gliding; the
# octave does not move and SHAPE does not open. Blended, the sound playing is the way between (an octave, a
# switch, at the middle), and it is saved with the journey, its A and B too. SOUNDS (LFO, from JOURNEY):
# SAVE stores the sound playing in a slot, SEL brings one back, gliding in. No clicks, no clips. Audio in
# absounds.wav.
wait 500
expect ab_have 0
tap ENV
turn K1 -20
tap HOME
press ENV
tap OCT-
release ENV
expect ab_have 1
expect view 0
tap ENV
turn K1 40
turn K4 30
tap HOME
key b1 down
turn K4 1
key b1 up
expect dvoice24 2
press ENV
tap OCT+
release ENV
expect ab_have 3
expect ab_t 127
expect view 0
expect shape11 115
wav absounds.wav
tapkey w4
press ENV
wait 700
turn SELECT -32 20
wait 2500
shot ab.png
release ENV
expect ab_t 0
expect shape11 35
expect shape14 44
expect dvoice24 1
expect view 0
press ENV
turn SELECT 16
wait 2500
release ENV
expect ab_t >60
expect ab_t <68
expect shape11 75
tap SAVE
wait 100
powercut
wait 500
expect ab_have 3
expect ab_t >60
expect shape11 75
tap LFO
tap LFO
expect view 7
tap SAVE
wait 100
expect snd1 1
tap ENV
turn K1 -30
expect shape11 15
tap LFO
tap LFO
tap SEL
wait 2500
shot sounds.png
expect shape11 75
tapkey w6
wait 3000
wavstop
expect clips 0
reboot
wait 300
expect snd1 1
